Pruning costs about 100–113 µs per file. The design will also store a per-file content hash, which lets `verify --rehash` check snapshots, so I need that hash's throughput for the budget.
[0m$ [0mcd /private/var/folders/k0/m1pgz3y90k34xd8h1b4tdkqw0000gp/T/opencode/backupctl-probe && PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 - <<'EOF'
import hashlib, time, json, os
buf = b"x" * (1 << 20)
N = 300
for name in ["blake2b", "sha256"]:
    t0 = time.perf_counter()
    h = hashlib.new(name) if name != "blake2b" else hashlib.blake2b(digest_size=16)
    for _ in range(N):
        h.update(buf)
    h.hexdigest()
    t1 = time.perf_counter()
    print(json.dumps({"mode": "hash_" + name, "MBps": round(N / (t1 - t0), 1)}))
EOF
